{"node_id": "NRS_484B_600_1c", "law_refs": ["NRS-484B-600-1c"], "subject": {"binder": "v", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "s1", "text": "It is unlawful for any person to drive or operate a vehicle of any kind or character at:", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "s2", "text": "A rate of speed greater than that posted by a public authority for the particular portion of highway being traversed.", "role": "obligation"}], "elements": [{"span": "s1", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": ["drv.motion.standstill"], "justification": "The same words as in NRS_484B_600_1a and read the same way: 'a vehicle of any kind or character' is the defined term the table resolves to DEF-NRS-484A-320, admitted as DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle, and ru.aggregate carries 'membership of a legal aggregate ... the atom's literal argument is an aggregate id'; 'to drive or operate' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion, drv.motion.standstill ('the road user is motionless at the observation: the magnitude of its velocity is at most the speed tolerance') read negated, a vehicle in motion being taken to be driven. Exclusions: ru.aggregate is not a stand-in for a class atom or a relational role; drv.motion.standstill is not a stand-in for the engine being off or a brake being applied, neither of which is read."}, {"span": "s2", "atoms": ["dev.governs", "dev.speed_limit_sign", "kin.speed", "rel.occupies", "st.highway", "st.on_way", "st.travel_region"], "derived": [], "justification": "kin.speed, 'magnitude of velocity', is the 'rate of speed'. dev.speed_limit_sign is a 'sign stating a maximum or minimum speed, with value and unit; kind in {maximum, minimum, structure_maximum, zone}', and its value for a sign of kind maximum, structure_maximum or zone is the speed 'posted ... for the particular portion of highway being traversed'. dev.governs, 'the travel regions whose traffic the device controls -- a lane, reserved lane, turn lane, centre turn lane, bicycle lane or path, roadway, one-way roadway or shoulder -- or an intersection', ties the sign to that portion: a travel region the subject's footprint overlaps (rel.occupies, 'a road user's footprint overlaps a lane / region'), quantified over st.travel_region, the kind dev.governs ranges over. st.on_way, 'the public way (a highway region) a structure region lies on', and st.highway, 'the entire public way between its boundary lines', carry 'of highway'. Exclusions: dev.governs is 'not a stand-in for a position', so dev.position is not read and no distance to the sign head is used; a sign of kind minimum is not read, the words forbidding only a speed greater than the posted one; st.travel_region is 'not a stand-in for the extent of a highway', which its own atom carries."}], "operationalizations": [], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [], "compositions": [], "residues": [], "binders": [], "applicability": "The subject vehicle v is in motion at the observation (drv.motion.standstill false for v, with p.standstill_speed_tolerance), which is how 'to drive or operate' is read, and some dev.speed_limit_sign of kind maximum, structure_maximum or zone governs (dev.governs) a travel region v's footprint overlaps (rel.occupies), that region lying on a highway (st.on_way, st.highway). Where no such sign governs a region v occupies, the duty does not arise.", "obligation": "v's speed (kin.speed) is at most the value of every such posted maximum: for each dev.speed_limit_sign of kind maximum, structure_maximum or zone governing a travel region v occupies, kin.speed does not exceed that sign's stated value, so the lowest posted maximum binds.", "params": ["p.standstill_speed_tolerance"], "narrowings": [{"span": "s1", "why": "'for any person to drive or operate' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion, as the ontology's section on what is not an atom directs: a vehicle moving on the road is taken to be driven, and the duty binds that vehicle's conduct whoever or whatever controls it.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}, {"span": "s2", "why": "'posted by a public authority' is read as the presence of the speed-limit sign on the road: the feature's presence is the observable evidence of its official posting, as the ontology directs for the legal status of a feature on the road. Which authority posted it, and its jurisdiction under DEF-NRS-484A-195, are not read.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "status"}, {"span": "s2", "why": "'the particular portion of highway being traversed' is read as a travel region the vehicle's footprint overlaps whose traffic the sign governs (dev.governs), that region lying on a highway; where several such signs govern regions the vehicle occupies, the lowest posted maximum binds. The posted maximum is read from signs of kind maximum, structure_maximum and zone, and a speed-limit sign carries no conditions attribute, so a legend stating hours or a class is read as a posting in effect.", "kind": "reading"}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A maximum-kind speed-limit sign governs the lane the subject occupies; the subject runs along that lane at a speed above the sign's stated value.", "masked": []}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "The same lane and the same governing maximum-kind sign; the subject's speed stays below the sign's stated value throughout. No other road user is present in the scene.", "masked": []}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "The subject runs along a highway on which the source records the governance of every device and no speed-limit sign governs any region the subject occupies, so no posted limit applies to the portion traversed.", "masked": []}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "The subject runs fast along a lane beside a sign head the source records, but the source does not observe speed-limit signs or their stated values, so whether a posted maximum is exceeded cannot be told.", "masked": ["dev.speed_limit_sign"]}, {"name": "branch_1", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "Two signs govern regions the subject occupies, a maximum-kind sign on the roadway and a lower zone-kind sign on the lane; the subject's speed lies between the two values, above the lower posted maximum.", "masked": []}, {"name": "branch_2", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "A minimum-kind speed-limit sign governs the lane the subject occupies and no other speed-limit sign does; the subject runs faster than that sign's stated value, which the words do not reach.", "masked": []}], "literals": [], "param_proposals": [], "gaps": []}
{"node_id": "NRS_484B_600_1e", "law_refs": ["NRS-484B-600-1e"], "subject": {"binder": "v", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "s1", "text": "It is unlawful for any person to drive or operate a vehicle of any kind or character at:", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "s2", "text": "In any event,", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s3", "text": "a rate of speed greater than 80 miles per hour.", "role": "obligation"}], "elements": [{"span": "s1", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": ["drv.motion.standstill"], "justification": "The same words as in NRS_484B_600_1a and NRS_484B_600_1c and read the same way: 'a vehicle of any kind or character' is the defined term the table resolves to DEF-NRS-484A-320, admitted as DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle, carried by ru.aggregate, whose 'literal argument is an aggregate id'; 'to drive or operate' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion, drv.motion.standstill read negated. Exclusions: ru.aggregate is not a stand-in for a class atom or a relational role; drv.motion.standstill is not a stand-in for the engine being off or a brake being applied."}, {"span": "s3", "atoms": ["kin.speed"], "derived": [], "justification": "kin.speed is the 'magnitude of velocity' in m/s, which is the 'rate of speed' the words bound; the bound is the figure the text itself states, declared as a literal in miles per hour on this span, and the comparison is that magnitude against it. Exclusion: kin.speed is the magnitude of velocity and not the acceleration along heading, which is not read; no posted sign and no judgement standard enters, the figure being the statute's own."}], "operationalizations": [], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [], "compositions": [], "residues": [{"span": "s2", "why": "The words add no observable condition and no restriction to the duty: they say that the cap binds whatever the other paragraphs of the subsection allow, so the duty is the same whether or not these words hold, and nothing in the scene is read for them.", "scope": "none"}], "binders": [], "applicability": "The subject vehicle v is in motion at the observation (drv.motion.standstill false for v, with p.standstill_speed_tolerance), which is how 'to drive or operate' is read: the duty binds the vehicle's conduct whoever or whatever is at the controls, in any event and wherever the vehicle runs.", "obligation": "v's speed (kin.speed) does not exceed the figure the text states, 80 miles per hour, carried as a literal in that unit.", "params": ["p.standstill_speed_tolerance"], "narrowings": [{"span": "s1", "why": "'for any person to drive or operate' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion, as the ontology's section on what is not an atom directs: a vehicle moving on the road is taken to be driven, and the duty binds that vehicle's conduct whoever or whatever controls it.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "The subject runs along an open highway at a speed above the figure the text states.", "masked": []}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "The subject runs along the same highway at a speed below the figure the text states, holding it for the whole recording. No other road user is present in the scene.", "masked": []}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "The subject stands in a parking bay with its engine running, the magnitude of its velocity within the standstill tolerance, so it is not driven or operated.", "masked": []}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "The subject is on the highway and the source supplies no magnitude of velocity for it, so neither whether it is in motion nor whether its speed exceeds the stated figure can be told.", "masked": ["kin.speed"]}], "literals": [{"span": "s3", "text": "80 miles per hour", "value": 80, "unit": "mph"}], "param_proposals": [], "gaps": []}
{"concept_id": "drv.motion.region_exit", "kind": "formula", "contract": "The road user's footprint ceases to overlap a structure region at the observation: it does not overlap the region at the observation and did overlap it at the observation before. The concept is the event of that ceasing to overlap, read at the observation at which the overlap has ended, and not the state of lying outside the region at the later observations. It states no direction of departure, no carrier the road user leaves through, no speed and no place outside the region. Not a stand-in for: lying outside the region, which the occupancy relation carries on its own; a later observation at which the road user is still outside; the carrier or the way the road user goes on to, which a caller reads with its own relations; a crossing of a boundary the source represents by no region; or an entry into the region, which has its own concept.", "definition": null, "args": [{"name": "u", "sort": "track"}, {"name": "r", "sort": "region"}], "params": [], "elements": [{"span": "it does not overlap the region at the observation and did overlap it at the observation before", "atoms": ["rel.occupies"], "concepts": [], "justification": "rel.occupies is 'a road user's footprint overlaps a lane / region (roadway, shoulder, sidewalk, intersection, crosswalk, stop line, safety zone, bicycle lane, median, alley, curb zone, controlled-access lane, structure)', which is the overlap the contract reads at the observation and at the one before; the region is the formal r the caller binds, so no region of the scene other than the one the caller singles out is read. Exclusion: the relation carries the footprint's overlap and not the geometry of the region (st.region_geometry), no distance being read, and not a direction or a speed of departure, which the contract expressly does not state."}], "residues": [], "literals": [], "scenarios": [{"name": "holds", "expected": "true", "narrative": "A vehicle's footprint overlaps an intersection region at one observation and, at the next, lies wholly clear of it: the concept holds at that next observation.", "masked": []}, {"name": "fails", "expected": "false", "narrative": "A vehicle's footprint overlaps the intersection region at both observations, having only moved farther into it: the concept fails. It fails as well at the observation after the departure, when the footprint lay clear of the region at the observation before.", "masked": []}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "The source does not observe which regions the vehicle's footprint overlaps, so whether the overlap with the region has just ended cannot be told.", "masked": ["rel.occupies"]}], "used_by": ["NRS_484B_400_2b"], "supersedes": null, "differs_from": {"concept": "drv.motion.region_entry", "why": "The sorts and the atom are the same as drv.motion.region_entry's, but the event is the opposite one: region_entry rises where the footprint comes to overlap the region, having not overlapped it at the observation before, while this concept rises where it ceases to overlap the region, having overlapped it at the observation before. Neither implies the other and no instantiation of one gives the other's verdict."}}

