e's conduct whoever or whatever controls it.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}, {"span": "s2", "why": "'posted by a public authority' is read as the presence of the speed-limit sign on the road: the feature's presence is the observable evidence of its official posting, as the ontology directs for the legal status of a feature on the road. Which authority posted it, and its jurisdiction under DEF-NRS-484A-195, are not read.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "status"}, {"span": "s2", "why": "'the particular portion of highway being traversed' is read as a travel region the vehicle's footprint overlaps whose traffic the sign governs (dev.governs), that region lying on a highway; where several such signs govern regions the vehicle occupies, the lowest posted maximum binds. The posted maximum is read from signs of kind maximum, structure_maximum and zone, and a speed-limit sign carries no conditions attribute, so a legend stating hours or a class is read as a posting in effect.", "kind": "reading"}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A maximum-kind speed-limit sign governs the lane the subject occupies; the subject runs along that lane at a speed above the sign's stated value.", "masked": []}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "The same lane and the same governing maximum-kind sign; the subject's speed stays below the sign's stated value throughout. No other road user is present in the scene.", "masked": []}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "The subject runs along a highway on which the source records the governance of every device and no speed-limit sign governs any region the subject occupies, so no posted limit applies to the portion traversed.", "masked": []}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "The subject runs fast along a lane beside a sign head the source records, but the source does not observe speed-limit signs or their stated values, so whether a posted maximum is exceeded cannot be told.", "masked": ["dev.speed_limit_sign"]}, {"name": "branch_1", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "Two signs govern regions the subject occupies, a maximum-kind sign on the roadway and a lower zone-kind sign on the lane; the subject's speed lies between the two values, above the lower posted maximum.", "masked": []}, {"name": "branch_2", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "A minimum-kind speed-limit sign governs the lane the subject occupies and no other speed-limit sign does; the subject runs faster than that sign's stated value, which the words do not reach.", "masked": []}], "literals": [], "param_proposals": [], "gaps": []}
{"node_id": "NRS_484B_600_1e", "law_refs": ["NRS-484B-600-1e"], "subject": {"binder": "v", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "s1", "text": "It is unlawful for any person to drive or operate a vehicle of any kind or character at:", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "s2", "text": "In any event,", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s3", "text": "a rate of speed greater than 80 miles per hour.", "role": "obligation"}], "elements": [{"span": "s1", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": ["drv.motion.standstill"], "justification": "The same words as in NRS_484B_600_1a and NRS_484B_600_1c and read the same way: 'a vehicle of any kind or character' is the defined term the table resolves to DEF-NRS-484A-320, admitted as DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle, carried by ru.aggregate, whose 'literal argument is an aggregate id'; 'to drive or operate' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion, drv.motion.standstill read negated. Exclusions: ru.aggregate is not a stand-in for a class atom or a relational role; drv.motion.standstill is not a stand-in for the engine being off or a brake being applied."}, {"span": "s3", "atoms": ["kin.speed"], "derived": [], "justification": "kin.speed is the 'magnitude of velocity' in m/s, which is the 'rate of speed' the words bound; the bound is the figure the text itself states, declared as a literal in miles per hour on this span, and the comparison is that magnitude against it. Exclusion: kin.speed is the magnitude of velocity and not the acceleration along heading, which is not read; no posted sign and no judgement standard enters, the figure being the statute's own."}], "operationalizations": [], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [], "compositions": [], "residues": [{"span": "s2", "why": "The words add no observable condition and no restriction to the duty: they say that the cap binds whatever the other paragraphs of the subsection allow, so the duty is the same whether or not these 